<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Banco Rio asks to issue $100 mln note.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Banco Rio asks to issue $100 mln note.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's Banco Rio de la Plata SA said Wednesday it has asked the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange for approval of the listing of a planned $100 million certificate issue.</p>
<p>The $100 million issue was given the go-ahead by the bank's directors on August 15. The issue is the second certificate under Banco Rio's short-term debt program approved at the beginning of the year.</p>
<p>The program has also been approved by Argentina's financial market watchdog, the Comision Nacional de Valores.</p>
<p>Banco Rio gave no further details of the timing or terms of the certificate issue.</p>
<p>-- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 3180668</p>
</text>
